{"title":"2002 IMO Shortlist Problems/C4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/C4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Bulgaria</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e04dadb5f6870434e79813f5ee568b1864df29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle T$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> be the set of ordered triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed3a16859e124e07d55752465af3d091302e69c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b5a07f2a22fcb2626031da734012c71b549782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4e6ba8781d42ee434379ac570532e425e7b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92f0f14d95ee05d626edff5beefd55475db83278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle z$\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" /> are integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/edd4bc0a6a246e5d55345acd16d793c8bcca2469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le x,y,z \\le 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />.  Players <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ef645c78704dbe5a136258a49d8425298f623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133465fc3d126a47593d2ffc76426cb2e5e9437d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle B$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> play the following game.  Player <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ef645c78704dbe5a136258a49d8425298f623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" /> chooses a triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed3a16859e124e07d55752465af3d091302e69c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e04dadb5f6870434e79813f5ee568b1864df29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle T$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />, and Player <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133465fc3d126a47593d2ffc76426cb2e5e9437d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle B$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> has to discover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ef645c78704dbe5a136258a49d8425298f623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" />'s triple in as few moves as possible.  A <i>move</i> consists of the following: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133465fc3d126a47593d2ffc76426cb2e5e9437d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle B$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ef645c78704dbe5a136258a49d8425298f623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" /> a triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e7369bc7279cd286b32ac6b2480458688a510938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e04dadb5f6870434e79813f5ee568b1864df29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle T$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ef645c78704dbe5a136258a49d8425298f623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" /> replies by giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133465fc3d126a47593d2ffc76426cb2e5e9437d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle B$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecf22d1a144e58f0aad4e61f12e5b438d1303c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle |x+y -a-b| + |y+z -b-c| + |z+x -c-a|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"381\" height=\"18\" />.  find the minimum number of moves that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133465fc3d126a47593d2ffc76426cb2e5e9437d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle B$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> needs to be sure of determining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ef645c78704dbe5a136258a49d8425298f623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" />'s triple.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/C4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In mod 2, we see that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0f6c2d8d3e56988861d8e922222c41b389c9e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle |x+y -a-b| + |y+z -b-c| + |z+x -c-a| \\equiv 2(x+y+z -a-b-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"599\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>so the outcome of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133465fc3d126a47593d2ffc76426cb2e5e9437d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle B$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />'s move must always be even.  Furthermore, the outcome must be no greater than 54 and no less than 0, so there are at most 28 different possible outcomes per move.  Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/185c7abc7ca92a5eaaec137d3e665f3bd432d165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 10^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> possible triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed3a16859e124e07d55752465af3d091302e69c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> and at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f139fc0357b21de1e8c0a045aaad255709ed2f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 28^2 &lt; 10^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> possible outcomes after two moves, at least three moves are required.\n</p><p>We will now show how to determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed3a16859e124e07d55752465af3d091302e69c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> in three moves.  A first move of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/f/a1fb598f55234f3cf3239626d489655a427e3c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (0,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> will give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce7ec54f31480d9447d47e986f762bb280d066dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 2(x+y+z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />.  We shall denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/f/d4fc423c05fa052e7d0e3ac5d5aebce7094449ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x+y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bc18328ddad852e8c812a5524cf3a0bd2fe6fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle s$\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb25528ed3f00e8466c0ae2b2f7ee6569de86a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\le 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, then the moves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/a/d2af045a94dad5333c88bd6a0453eeec0eb60749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (9,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/6/9e6afd83dab61ac2d364ad16cac5a8f66a70d6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (0,9,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> will give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/98155968d3e7073e895177a7b2340dfaf79c171f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 18 -2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d65868c7b96fa0f1becd1bfc1fe23a124a85192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 18 - 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, respectively, enabling us to determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed3a16859e124e07d55752465af3d091302e69c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />.  Similarly, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/667e1b16c74f6f29f39f9c57a9f393557c2ab427.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\ge 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, the moves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d16d28a0b0dec8b92cefbb5a289f49427a64a69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (0,9,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d9424ec87bbb4a0e4cd13a17227ce3b3b850ad97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (9,0,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> will give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de187b3ec660fa34a134fe95b7d299ccdc77ea8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d2828e58fde892b4c8fb50831ae91908dc163d5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8e1a268e2e2d89d628a59e0b635b72b78b755c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 9 &lt; s &lt; 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />, then our second move is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62c20dae4ba0cf764472f54b1b31f60ee5c8755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (9, s-9, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />.  Let us call the result <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/0095d10fed9dccbdc8ed62bdb83bda276ca7186b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />.  We have two cases.  In Case I, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/2/f32cd28e6f838e152abe7d295b0f73662fac2c5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle y &gt; s-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a4837d97fb646f6696630a8e1d8c7369c0b9b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x = 9-k$\" width=\"75\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a34e60dfc126802aa2efb923daabb4116ee36a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle z&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />.  In Case II, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c046d4817b3f5bee00236ec7f360c657aaff199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\le s-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cdaf4e8a8aa13477a965b246d43b0ec46a9e37d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x \\ge 9-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/90622fd1f2e8ae094aba3cc9abfb9fa3a86a967f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle z=k$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.  In either case, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/f/d9f9dcfab5d967d1f679f4099bd955d5244356a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle z \\le k \\le y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" /> (the right-hand side comes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/775f475a303cf86fe7368a7931d3005a32e8cf98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle y+z = s-9 +k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8acfddefcf2b6c7b452ee0f26daafe4050572dff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=k , y \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f4d421e821218b004e5a83add3e5587f9e940fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+z \\le 9 + k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Now, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88ca3343be603bd7139ae7a6d824b8ab6095129e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-k \\le 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />, then our third move is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feb1d76e34f9fea0d0ccfc6ea99b0b60cc46a017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (s-k, 0, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />.  This gives us\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8184f5227f6f95df5e5e8c71e0496d7488a4edb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle |x+y - s+k| + |y+z -k| + |z+x - s| = k-z + y+z-k + y = 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"561\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4e6ba8781d42ee434379ac570532e425e7b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" /> and tells us whether Case I or Case II holds, letting us determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed3a16859e124e07d55752465af3d091302e69c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>On the other hand, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8cebaacb710ecf0203669e3c2c024b9574354a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle s-k &gt; 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />, our third move is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe5768fa1e3af1b596e6b5ea72493f5fb35e922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (9, s-k-9, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />.  This gives us\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b13e2dec2427006ee65d15c34fe83d402f335f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle |x+y -s+k| + |y+z -s+9| + |z+x -k-9| = |k-z| + |9-x| + |k+9 -z-x| = 2(k+9-s+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"826\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>which again gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4e6ba8781d42ee434379ac570532e425e7b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" />, telling us which of Cases I and II hold, letting us determine the triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed3a16859e124e07d55752465af3d091302e69c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/C4&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/C4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2002 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2002 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=118715#p118715\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018045544\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 345/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 353/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 12017/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.319      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.319      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4843:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018045544 and revision id 14392. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}